      "content": "Let’s use a similar example first:\n\n$$ (3x + 6)(x - 2) = 0 $$\n\nIf two factors multiply to give zero, at least one factor must be zero. So we set each bracket equal to zero:\n\n$$3x + 6 = 0 \\quad\\text{or}\\quad x - 2 = 0$$\n\nSolving gives $x = -2$ or $x = 2$.\n\nNow apply the same first step to your equation, $(2x - 3)(x + 7) = 0$. What equation do you get by setting the first bracket equal to zero?"
    },
